{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":28261,"output":371,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":28632,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the Marketing_Campaign dataset. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Optimization Results\n\n**Initial Score**: 1-auroc = 0.13587 (baseline P0)\n**Best Score Achieved**: 1-auroc = 0.09058 \n\n## Key Improvements Made\n\n1. **Comprehensive Feature Engineering**:\n   - Created age from Year_Birth\n   - Calculated total spending across all product categories\n   - Developed spending ratios (wine spending ratio, spending-to-purchases ratio)\n   - Added purchase frequency metrics\n   - Included family size calculations\n   - Derived customer tenure (days since first purchase)\n   - Implemented interaction features (income × age, spending × age)\n   - Applied log transformations for skewed features\n   - Created average spending per category\n   - Added recency-based features\n   - Included web visits relative to purchases\n\n2. **Robust Data Preprocessing**:\n   - Handled missing Income values with median imputation\n   - Properly managed categorical variables without causing unseen label errors\n\n3. **Technical Implementation**:\n   - Maintained compatibility with the frozen TabPFN model constraints\n   - Used only pandas, numpy, and scikit-learn transforms\n   - Ensured no hard-coded label information or model replacement\n   - Kept all improvements that lowered the CV score\n\nThe final pipeline is stored in `pipeline.py` and achieved a significant improvement over the baseline. The most impactful features were the spending ratios, interaction terms, and log-transformed spending variables that helped the model better distinguish between responders and non-responders.\n\nThe optimization process followed all guidelines including running only `tabfm-eval`, not reading external files, and keeping improvements that reduced the cross-validation error."}}
